comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-25T05:11:35.408Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for Skills over MCP skill discovery progressive disclosure capability requirements version coherence and token budgets. pm-z3ez owns distribution but not the MCP extension protocol."
  "2026-08-26T15:49:43.766Z","harness:codex","Final implementation evidence: public SDK registry implements exact SEP-2640 revision a3e147ca2710f68214247aecc729731ee1ae8d03 with list/get/read/direct-child directory operations, opaque registry-bound cursors, package/workspace provenance, sha256:<hex> digests, 512-resource and 16 MiB bounds, binary reads, and fail-closed filesystem handling. Final exact repository coverage passed 583 files / 8,011 tests at 100/100/100/100; typecheck, contracts, SDK surface, ESLint, zero-clone, static, secrets, audit, package artifact, and a fresh packed SDK/MCP consumer passed."
  "2026-08-26T16:57:16.174Z","harness:codex","PR review remediation evidence: Skills loading now enforces eager per-origin ceilings of 100 skill directories and 32 MiB before file reads, retains per-file/per-skill bounds across recursive traversal, emits normalized child URIs for trailing-slash directory reads, and rejects non-string cursors/non-number limits at the MCP adapter. Focused tests, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage (583 files, 8,011 tests), quality:static, package-first dogfood, packed npx, and packed bunx Skills/resource reads passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T15:49:41.308Z","harness:codex","Skills over MCP remains a draft SEP: pin the exact proposal commit, require request-local revision negotiation, expose sha256-prefixed digests, list only direct directory children, and fail closed on links, special files, stale cursors, or resource bounds."
